WEBVTT

1
00:00:31.916 --> 00:00:36.250


2
00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:39.375
<b>Lord Krishna has shared many teachings,</b>

3
00:00:39.375 --> 00:00:41.833
<b>particularly about selfless action </b>
<b>(Nishkama Karma Yoga).</b>

4
00:00:41.833 --> 00:00:47.708
<b>He spoke of (raag) meaning excessive </b>
<b>attachment and (dvesh) meaning intense hatred,</b>

5
00:00:47.708 --> 00:00:50.500
<b>We need to be staying away from both.</b>

6
00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:53.750
<b>Upon hearing this, one might resolve,</b>

7
00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:57.625
<b>"From today, I shall neither be</b>
<b>attached nor harbor hatred...</b>

8
00:00:57.625 --> 00:01:00.958
<b>I will only perform selfless actions."</b>

9
00:01:00.958 --> 00:01:01.750
<b>We</b>

10
00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:05.500
<b>often make such resolutions to control ourselves.</b>

11
00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:09.875
<b>Yet, we soon find ourselves </b>
<b>sliding back into old patterns.</b>

12
00:01:09.875 --> 00:01:13.250
<b>Despite our intentions, we become </b>
<b>participants in wrongful acts.</b>

13
00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:14.666
<b>Why does this happen?</b>

14
00:01:14.666 --> 00:01:19.250
<b>In this verse, Arjuna raises precisely this question.</b>

15
00:01:19.875 --> 00:01:24.041


16
00:01:24.041 --> 00:01:25.708
<b>Arjuna asks,</b>

17
00:01:25.708 --> 00:01:26.958
<b>"Krishna,</b>

18
00:01:26.958 --> 00:01:31.708
<b>why does a person get driven to </b>
<b>wrongful actions even against their will?</b>

19
00:01:31.708 --> 00:01:33.416
<b>It appears as though</b>

20
00:01:33.416 --> 00:01:39.541
<b>they are being forcefully compelled to </b>
<b>perform such acts, even when they don't wish to. </b>

21
00:01:39.541 --> 00:01:44.291
<b>What drives us to perform </b>
<b>impure and sinful actions?"</b>

22
00:01:44.291 --> 00:01:46.500
<b>You must have observed this too –</b>

23
00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:48.208
<b>someone becomes angry,</b>

24
00:01:48.208 --> 00:01:51.000
<b>and in that heated moment, speaks</b>

25
00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.458
<b>or acts harmfully,</b>

26
00:01:52.458 --> 00:01:57.333
<b>only to reflect later with regret, saying,</b>

27
00:01:57.333 --> 00:01:59.291
<b>"Why did I do this?</b>

28
00:01:59.291 --> 00:02:05.583
<b>I can't believe I was the one who said </b>
<b>and did such terrible things."</b>

29
00:02:05.583 --> 00:02:08.666
<b>Perhaps you've experienced this yourself.</b>

30
00:02:08.666 --> 00:02:12.583
<b>That's why when we see someone in anger,</b>

31
00:02:12.583 --> 00:02:15.625
<b>we say they're "not themselves."</b>

32
00:02:15.625 --> 00:02:17.583
<b>But then, under whose influence are they?</b>

33
00:02:17.583 --> 00:02:19.916
<b>Is the Divine making this happen?</b>

34
00:02:19.916 --> 00:02:22.708
<b>But the Divine wishes for our wellbeing,</b>

35
00:02:22.708 --> 00:02:25.166
<b>so why would They push us toward wrongdoing?</b>

36
00:02:25.166 --> 00:02:27.958
<b>And if it's not the Divine,</b>

37
00:02:27.958 --> 00:02:30.125
<b>then how is this happening?</b>

38
00:02:30.125 --> 00:02:33.875
<b>The upcoming verses will address </b>
<b>this very question.</b>

39
00:02:34.416 --> 00:02:38.250


40
00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:44.583
<b>This teaching deeply resonates</b>
<b>with our personal lives.</b>

41
00:02:44.583 --> 00:02:48.166
<b>Often, we find ourselves in situations</b>

42
00:02:48.166 --> 00:02:52.750
<b>where anger takes over, relationships break,</b>

43
00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:58.333
<b>or we do something we later regret.</b>

44
00:02:58.333 --> 00:03:01.458
<b>Then comes that haunting question:</b>

45
00:03:01.458 --> 00:03:03.541
<b>"How could I do this?"</b>

46
00:03:03.541 --> 00:03:06.041
<b>"I must be a terrible person."</b>

47
00:03:06.041 --> 00:03:11.333
<b>In those moments, it feels as if we </b>
<b>completely lost control of ourselves.</b>

48
00:03:11.333 --> 00:03:19.875
<b>Generally, this happens because </b>
<b>of our inner desires and beliefs.</b>

49
00:03:19.875 --> 00:03:25.416
<b>Understanding this calmly will help us grow.</b>

50
00:03:25.416 --> 00:03:27.083
<b>First,</b>

51
00:03:27.083 --> 00:03:30.875
<b>don't hate yourself.</b>

52
00:03:30.875 --> 00:03:33.583
<b>Everyone loses control –</b>

53
00:03:33.583 --> 00:03:35.000
<b>sometimes a little,</b>

54
00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:36.791
<b>sometimes more.</b>

55
00:03:36.791 --> 00:03:42.541
<b>This doesn't mean your </b>
<b>actions weren't wrong – they were.</b>

56
00:03:42.541 --> 00:03:43.458
<b>But</b>

57
00:03:43.458 --> 00:03:50.541
<b>if a teacher starts hating their</b>
<b>student for making mistakes,</b>

58
00:03:50.541 --> 00:03:53.541
<b>the learning becomes impossible.</b>

59
00:03:53.541 --> 00:03:54.791
<b>Here,</b>

60
00:03:54.791 --> 00:03:56.875
<b>you are both the teacher</b>

61
00:03:56.875 --> 00:03:59.250
<b>and the student.</b>

62
00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:02.375
<b>So don't harbor self-hatred.</b>

63
00:04:02.375 --> 00:04:06.083
<b>Become your own teacher –</b>

64
00:04:06.083 --> 00:04:10.166
<b>reflect deeply and understand</b>

65
00:04:10.166 --> 00:04:13.458
<b>what was happening inside you at that moment.</b>

66
00:04:13.458 --> 00:04:15.125
<b>What thoughts</b>

67
00:04:15.125 --> 00:04:17.250
<b>were running through your mind?</b>

68
00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:20.708
<b>What specifically triggered you?</b>

69
00:04:20.708 --> 00:04:25.583
<b>Through this self-reflection, when similar </b>
<b>situations arise in the future,</b>

70
00:04:25.583 --> 00:04:28.583
<b>you'll be more aware.</b>

71
00:04:28.583 --> 00:04:36.458
<b>You'll also become better at recognizing signs</b>
<b>of agitation within yourself.</b>

72
00:04:36.458 --> 00:04:39.833
<b>When you notice these signs,</b>

73
00:04:39.833 --> 00:04:43.791
<b>take a step back,</b>

74
00:04:43.791 --> 00:04:45.833
<b>breathe deeply,</b>

75
00:04:45.833 --> 00:04:51.375
<b>and pause your reaction just for a few moments.</b>

76
00:04:51.375 --> 00:04:56.000
<b>Like a wave that rises and falls,</b>

77
00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:04.041
<b>your surge of emotion will naturally calm down.</b>

78
00:05:04.041 --> 00:05:07.791
<b>And remember this –</b>

79
00:05:07.791 --> 00:05:10.333
<b>everyone makes mistakes.</b>

80
00:05:10.333 --> 00:05:14.416
<b>It's an integral part of being human.</b>

81
00:05:14.416 --> 00:05:21.166
<b>So whenever you make an error, </b>
<b>don't condemn yourself.</b>

82
00:05:21.166 --> 00:05:28.291
<b>Instead, gently consider </b>
<b>why the mistake happened</b>

83
00:05:28.291 --> 00:05:33.333
<b>and what can be done to prevent it in the future.</b>

84
00:05:33.333 --> 00:05:34.791
<b>Remember,</b>

85
00:05:34.791 --> 00:05:41.958
<b>the goal is continuous learning </b>
<b>and self – improvement.</b>

86
00:05:41.958 --> 00:05:49.750
<b>The goal is not perfection in every situation,</b>

87
00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:54.541
<b>as that's impossible for any human.</b>

88
00:05:54.541 --> 00:05:57.833
<b> Keep evaluating yourself,</b>

89
00:05:57.833 --> 00:06:00.916
<b>remain gentle with yourself,</b>

90
00:06:00.916 --> 00:06:03.958
<b>and keep moving toward improvement.</b>

91
00:06:04.541 --> 00:06:08.416


92
00:06:08.458 --> 00:06:10.750
<b>Without a doubt,</b>

93
00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:16.333
<b>relationships in a family setting</b>
<b>are incredibly close.</b>

94
00:06:16.333 --> 00:06:20.875
<b>While this enriches our lives with sweetness,</b>

95
00:06:20.875 --> 00:06:30.666
<b>it also means we feel deep remorse when we </b>
<b>commit a mistake or hurt someone’s feelings.</b>

96
00:06:30.666 --> 00:06:38.291
<b>Sometimes in stressful moments, </b>
<b>we lash out at our spouse or children,</b>

97
00:06:38.291 --> 00:06:39.916
<b>say hurtful things,</b>

98
00:06:39.916 --> 00:06:45.458
<b>or neglect family members due to being busy.</b>

99
00:06:45.458 --> 00:06:50.875
<b>And later, we're filled with regret thinking,</b>

100
00:06:50.875 --> 00:06:53.750
<b>"You shouldn't have done that."</b>

101
00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:55.000
<b>Yet,</b>

102
00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:58.875
<b>the situation repeats itself.</b>

103
00:06:58.875 --> 00:07:03.333
<b>And again comes the self-reproach.</b>

104
00:07:03.333 --> 00:07:05.541
<b>Why does this happen?</b>

105
00:07:05.541 --> 00:07:08.416
<b>Can it be changed?</b>

106
00:07:08.416 --> 00:07:10.208
<b>Know this -</b>

107
00:07:10.208 --> 00:07:13.541
<b>humans are emotional beings.</b>

108
00:07:13.541 --> 00:07:16.416
<b>We all make such mistakes.</b>

109
00:07:16.416 --> 00:07:18.083
<b>So first -</b>

110
00:07:18.083 --> 00:07:21.083
<b>stop blaming yourself.</b>

111
00:07:21.083 --> 00:07:21.875
<b>Now,</b>

112
00:07:21.875 --> 00:07:25.125
<b>move toward change.</b>

113
00:07:25.125 --> 00:07:29.125
<b>Any improvement requires change,</b>

114
00:07:29.125 --> 00:07:34.875
<b>and change requires self-awareness</b>
<b>and self-reflection.</b>

115
00:07:34.875 --> 00:07:39.250
<b>When we look within, we'll realize</b>

116
00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:48.625
<b>that our adverse reactions stem mainly </b>
<b>from our inner conflicts and unresolved tensions.</b>

117
00:07:48.625 --> 00:07:55.000
<b>Understanding this is the next step</b>
<b>toward creating a better family environment.</b>

118
00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:57.958
<b>Then - it's essential</b>

119
00:07:57.958 --> 00:08:05.083
<b>to examine those situations when </b>
<b>you unintentionally hurt someone.</b>

120
00:08:05.083 --> 00:08:07.583
<b>What happened in that moment?</b>

121
00:08:07.583 --> 00:08:08.458
<b>Why</b>

122
00:08:08.458 --> 00:08:11.875
<b>did you lose control?</b>

123
00:08:11.875 --> 00:08:16.916
<b>What was truly important </b>
<b>at that time - your work,</b>

124
00:08:16.916 --> 00:08:21.583
<b>or perhaps giving time to your child?</b>

125
00:08:21.583 --> 00:08:23.541
<b>Remember,</b>

126
00:08:23.541 --> 00:08:26.875
<b>these thoughts aren't for self-condemnation,</b>

127
00:08:26.875 --> 00:08:31.541
<b>but only for better self-understanding.</b>

128
00:08:31.541 --> 00:08:35.041
<b>As you understand yourself this way,</b>

129
00:08:35.041 --> 00:08:38.833
<b>you'll become more conscious in the future,</b>

130
00:08:38.833 --> 00:08:42.500
<b>and gradually, change will come.</b>

131
00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:45.750
<b>There's another beautiful aspect to this –</b>

132
00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:51.750
<b>when you begin to understand </b>
<b>the inner causes of your reactions,</b>

133
00:08:51.750 --> 00:09:00.000
<b>you'll also understand that </b>
<b>when others get irritated with you,</b>

134
00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:03.958
<b>their intention isn't to hurt you – </b>

135
00:09:03.958 --> 00:09:11.708
<b>infact they too are acting from their </b>
<b>inner tensions.</b>

136
00:09:11.708 --> 00:09:18.541
<b>This understanding teaches </b>
<b>both empathy and forgiveness,</b>

137
00:09:18.541 --> 00:09:24.791
<b>and for family love, these are like nectar.</b>

138
00:09:24.791 --> 00:09:26.875
<b>Now imagine</b>

139
00:09:26.875 --> 00:09:33.750
<b>what would happen if such thinking </b>
<b>were encouraged in families.</b>

140
00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:39.958
<b>Everyone would treat each other with empathy,</b>

141
00:09:39.958 --> 00:09:49.375
<b>even after mistakes, bitterness wouldn't</b>
<b>linger long. Only love would remain.</b>

142
00:09:49.375 --> 00:09:53.875
<b>How sweet such a family would be.</b>

143
00:09:53.875 --> 00:09:55.250
<b>Think about it.</b>

144
00:09:55.750 --> 00:09:59.541


145
00:09:59.541 --> 00:10:04.958
<b>Have you ever experienced such a day at work –</b>

146
00:10:04.958 --> 00:10:10.833
<b>when you got into an argument with </b>
<b>a colleague over something trivial?</b>

147
00:10:10.833 --> 00:10:15.333
<b>Or made a wrong decision</b>

148
00:10:15.333 --> 00:10:20.166
<b>you would never make in a normal state of mind?</b>

149
00:10:20.166 --> 00:10:25.041
<b>And then, in solitude, you wondered,</b>

150
00:10:25.041 --> 00:10:27.250
<b>"How did this happen?"</b>

151
00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:31.958
<b>As if in those moments, you had </b>
<b>completely lost your self-control.</b>

152
00:10:31.958 --> 00:10:39.625
<b>This can happen not just in family situations, </b>
<b>but in professional settings too.</b>

153
00:10:39.625 --> 00:10:41.458
<b>Perhaps</b>

154
00:10:41.458 --> 00:10:44.750
<b>it's a personal feeling of insecurity,</b>

155
00:10:44.750 --> 00:10:50.125
<b>the pressure of an approaching </b>
<b>deadline for unfinished work,</b>

156
00:10:50.125 --> 00:10:54.500
<b>a workload beyond your capacity,</b>

157
00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:59.250
<b>or an urge to diminish others –</b>

158
00:10:59.250 --> 00:11:01.791
<b>there can be many reasons.</b>

159
00:11:01.791 --> 00:11:04.750
<b>But one thing is certain –</b>

160
00:11:04.750 --> 00:11:08.583
<b>these reasons usually aren't external,</b>

161
00:11:08.583 --> 00:11:12.000
<b>but lie within you.</b>

162
00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:14.958
<b>And if the causes are within you,</b>

163
00:11:14.958 --> 00:11:20.916
<b>expecting others to change would be a mistake.</b>

164
00:11:20.916 --> 00:11:26.708
<b>Looking within yourself is a major </b>
<b>step toward the solution.</b>

165
00:11:26.708 --> 00:11:30.208
<b>Understanding the real cause is the second step.</b>

166
00:11:30.208 --> 00:11:35.291
<b>Why did you lose control in that moment?</b>

167
00:11:35.291 --> 00:11:38.625
<b>The solution will emerge from this understanding.</b>

168
00:11:38.625 --> 00:11:40.166
<b>For example...</b>

169
00:11:40.166 --> 00:11:46.500
<b>you notice a pattern that whenever </b>
<b>work pressure becomes excessive,</b>

170
00:11:46.500 --> 00:11:49.416
<b>you get angry quickly.</b>

171
00:11:49.416 --> 00:11:54.541
<b>Just this self-awareness will </b>
<b>partially solve the problem.</b>

172
00:11:54.541 --> 00:11:58.000
<b>You'll naturally be more alert next time.</b>

173
00:11:58.000 --> 00:12:04.750
<b>Taking one step further,</b>
<b>you can adopt other measures,</b>

174
00:12:04.750 --> 00:12:11.041
<b>like going for a morning walk daily, </b>
<b>especially on stressful days,</b>

175
00:12:11.041 --> 00:12:17.750
<b>and taking a few moments every hour</b>
<b>at work to breathe deeply.</b>

176
00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:22.875
<b>Big problems often solve themselves </b>
<b>through small solutions.</b>

177
00:12:22.875 --> 00:12:26.125
<b>You just need to be aware of the problem.</b>

178
00:12:26.125 --> 00:12:27.208
<b>And yes –</b>

179
00:12:27.208 --> 00:12:32.250
<b>losing control like this isn't unusual.</b>
<b>It happens to everyone.</b>

180
00:12:32.250 --> 00:12:33.583
<b>However,</b>

181
00:12:33.583 --> 00:12:36.833
<b>reflecting on such incidents</b>

182
00:12:36.833 --> 00:12:44.291
<b>and improving yourself can certainly </b>
<b>make your growth unusual.</b>

183
00:12:44.291 --> 00:12:46.041
<b>Think about it.</b>

